          "question": "What happens if the score is high?",
          "answer": "I couldn't find anything about what happens when an anxiety questionnaire score is high. The passages returned don't say how anxiety scores are interpreted or what follows from them.\n\nOne returned passage describes how a questionnaire is used in COPD, a lung condition. It says the questionnaire result, along with the past year's flare-ups, helps place a person in a group that guides starting treatment. That describes COPD care only, so I can't apply it to anxiety. Another passage, from a document with a COPD title, discusses how exercise can cause racing heart rate and sweating that people with anxiety may misread. It doesn't mention scores.\n\nThe safety check found no emergency pattern in what you described. That doesn't mean there is no risk. If your anxiety gets worse, or you have thoughts of harming yourself, contact emergency services or a crisis line now.\n\nA doctor or nurse can explain what a score means for you and what options follow from it. Tell them anxiety is affecting your work.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
